READ (the maintainer's criterion -- asymptotic convergence, not finite-n perfection):
  |trace - 1| SHRINKING with n  => consistent; finite-n bias is not a defect.
  |trace - 1| GROWING with n    => persists asymptotically; a real estimator problem,
                                   OR the estimand is mis-declared ([[LESSONS]]:784).
  Latent-r is NOT expected to improve with n: each unit's score is an INCIDENTAL
  parameter (more units = more parameters, not more information per unit). It should
  improve with p instead -- that is dev/va-usability/60-binomial-p-ladder.R.

